<title>FRANCE: New York top destination for Paris Jan 97 cargo exports.</title>
<headline>New York top destination for Paris Jan 97 cargo exports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority, the Aeroports de Paris (ADP), said New York was the top export destination from Charles de Gaulle and Orly Airports in January 1997.</p>
<p>The top ten destinations for ADP exports for January 1997 in tonnes and with percentage change on January 1996, were as follows:</p>
<p> 1  New York	    2,378    down  4.2pct</p>
<p> 2  Chicago	     1,904    up   11.7</p>
<p> 3  Tokyo		 1,787    down 19.2</p>
<p> 4  Hong Kong	   1,466    down 15.1</p>
<p> 5  Sao Paulo	   1,024    up   65.9</p>
<p> 6  Montreal		921    down 20.2</p>
<p> 7  Singapore	     904    up   43.4</p>
<p> 8  Mexico City	   783    down 16.3</p>
<p> 9  Dubai		   706    up    7.0</p>
<p> 10 Seoul		   643    up   14.7</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
</text>
